    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0635" n="615" xml:id="pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/8–2150</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Counselor</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Deputy Under
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-08-21">August 21, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I approve generally of the considerations set forth in Mr. Jessup’s memorandum of
                    August 17 about our position with respect to an eventual proposal for withdrawal
                    of United Nations forces concurrent with the withdrawal of the North Korean
                    forces to the 38th Parallel.</p>
                <p>I am not sure that we will have to insist on United Nations supervision of
                    elections “throughout Korea”. I think it may be necessary to return to the
                    divided status, leaving South Korea as a sort of U.N. trusteeship, protected by
                    forces of other U.N. nations, under U.N. control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi> F. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
